  "term": "thrombotic stroke",
  "definition": "Thrombotic stroke is an ischemic stroke caused when a blood clot forms inside an artery in the brain and blocks blood flow. It is often linked with atherosclerosis and does not include strokes caused by clots in brain veins.",
